  "rationale": "structural: `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.doctests` has one clause: the bundled agent instructions \"MUST direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". This clause fixes what the instructions say, not how any code is built. It names no library, algorithm, signature, type or delegation. The only structural reading is that the instruction text must exist in the bundled instruction files. The supplied roots are those files, and each one carries the directive:\n- `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` says, in the \"Testing and coverage artifacts\" section, \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n- `assets/skills/habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` says, in \"Testing and coverage findings\", \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n- `assets/skills/habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md` says the same sentence in its \"Bootstrap requirements\" section.\n- `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md` says \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n\nI relied on search excerpts of these four passages and did not read the files in full. I found no structural obligation without implementation evidence, so no root is missing. Whether tests check the wording is a behavioral question and is outside this assessment.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has one observable obligation. The bundled agent instructions must direct agents to run Cargo doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`.\n\n`tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[bundled_skills_default_to_process_coverage_and_keep_artifacts_disposable]` is marked `{test}` for `requirements.test-coverage.guidance.doctests`. It checks that obligation in three ways.\n\n- **Each coverage-related skill:** for `habeas`, `habeas-evidence` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements`, it asserts that the whitespace-normalized text contains `` `cargo test --doc --workspace` ``.\n- **Directive wording:** it asserts the exact directive sentences. The `habeas` skill must say \"Run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\". The evidence and bootstrap skills must say \"run doctests separately with `cargo test --doc --workspace`\".\n- **SOP:** it also asserts the same sentence in `agent-sops/approved-implementation.sop.md`.\n\nThe search results show that the skill text contains these directives. They appear in the Testing and coverage artifacts section of `assets/skills/habeas/SKILL.md` and in the paragraphs of `habeas-evidence/SKILL.md` and `habeas-bootstrap-requirements/SKILL.md`. These assertions would fail if a skill dropped the directive or lost the word \"separately\".\n\nThe text of `habeas-requirements` and `habeas-refactor` has no doctest guidance, and the test does not check those two skills. Those two skills cover requirement authoring and refactoring, not test or coverage runs. The requirement does not clearly extend to them, so I treat the three test-running skills as the intended scope and report no gap.",
